  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nUpper level trough has moved in with drier NW flow in place. \nSome moisture around today will help a few light rain showers \ndevelop, mainly across higher terrain of CNY and the Catskills. \nDay time highs in the low to mid 70s and morning lows in the low\n50s and upper 40s will make it feel a bit more fall like over \nthe next few days. Fog formation in the deeper river valleys of \nthe Twin Tiers and Catskills is likely the next few nights. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nUpper level ridging looks to briefly build back in Tuesday into\nWednesday with temperatures warming back above normal. A \nstronger low pressure system forms in the lee of the northern \nRockies and moves north of the Great Lakes Wednesday into \nThursday. The low has trended a little weaker and farther north \nso the cold front associated with it is not as strong as \nprevious days. Still, there is some model agreement of some \ninstability and shear ahead of it so if the frontal passage can \nbe in the afternoon on Wednesday then there is a chance for some\nstronger storms. Timing is still uncertain with the frontal \npassage as the ensemble peak CAPE + Shear bullseye is more in \nthe Ohio River Valley into western NY.",
